# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local build scratch. Everything under artifacts/ that CI publishes is committed;
# these are intermediates that are not.
_work/
*.tmp

# The map from the STS back to the markdown that produced it — line numbers, written by
# `build` beside the STS the way a .pdb is written beside an assembly, and read by `publish`
# to put a link to the source beside every clause.
#
# A handshake between two commands of one tool, and not an artifact: the published HTML
# already carries everything a reader needs. Committing it would add a file that churns on
# every line anyone inserts and that nothing outside this repository reads.
*.stsmap.json

# Visual Studio's local state. Its FileContentIndex holds files open, so git cannot
# even read them to decide they should be ignored.
.vs/
